# Every `:?`-guarded value below must be filled in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# State — absolute host paths
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These three previously read ${HOME}/... inline in the compose file, which is
# expanded by the INVOKING SHELL, not by Docker. One `sudo docker compose up`
# and ${HOME} becomes /root: Jellyfin starts with an empty config, re-scans the
# library as a fresh install, and the real config sits untouched in your home
# directory looking fine. Absolute paths remove the failure mode entirely.
#
# Do not change them on an existing deployment unless you move the data first.
JELLYFIN_DATA_PATH=
JELLYFIN_CONFIG_PATH=
JELLYFIN_CACHE_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media library — read-only, mounted as <MEDIA_PATH>/{shows,movies,music}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEDIA_PATH=/mnt/storage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ports: host networking, so 8096/tcp (web), 7359/udp (client discovery) and
# 1900/udp (DLNA SSDP) bind straight on the host and are not remappable from
# here. Nothing else in this repo claims them.
#
# Metrics: not scraped. host networking and the external `monitoring` network
# are mutually exclusive, and DLNA needs the former. Logs and container metrics
# still reach Alloy through the Docker socket.
#
# Hardware transcoding: not configured. It needs a `devices:` entry for
# /dev/dri plus the render group, and the container must be able to see the GPU.
